## std::rand — CSPRNG-backed random_bytes / random_u64 / random_fill.
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — first stdlib module fully migrated from
## resolve/stdlib/mod.rs Rust registrations into a self-hosted
## library/std/src/*.rx file. The signatures here ARE the source
## of truth that the resolver, typeck, MIR, and codegen consult.
##
## Per-platform CSPRNG backend (compile-time `#if` in
## library/runtime/io/rand.c): Linux `getrandom`, macOS
## `SecRandomCopyBytes` (`-framework Security` at link), fallback
## /dev/urandom.
##
## The byte-array carrier is `Array[Int]` (matching File.read_all /
## TcpStream.read), even though the user-facing spec spelling is
## `Array[U8]`. See docs/specs/stdlib/rand.spec.md.

## std::rand namespace class — 3 static methods. Phase C of #06.95.
## The bare lib block below is the transition shim keeping
## `random_bytes(n)` / `random_u64()` / `random_fill(buf)` resolving
## while existing callers migrate to `Rand.random_bytes(n)` / …
class Rand
  lib "runtime/rand.c"
    def self.random_bytes as "ruxen_rand_random_bytes"(n: Int) -> Result[Array[Int], IoError]
    def self.random_u64 as "ruxen_rand_random_u64"() -> Int
    def self.random_fill as "ruxen_rand_random_fill"(buf: &var Array[Int]) -> Result[(), IoError]
  end
end

# Phase C transition shim — see comment on `class Rand` above.
lib "runtime/rand.c"
  def random_bytes as "ruxen_rand_random_bytes"(n: Int) -> Result[Array[Int], IoError]
  def random_u64 as "ruxen_rand_random_u64"() -> Int
  def random_fill as "ruxen_rand_random_fill"(buf: &var Array[Int]) -> Result[(), IoError]
end
